cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "SyncAI-Lib-HydraNet: multi-task perception for fixed store CCTV"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - name: SYNCROBOTIC
repository-code: "https://github.com/Syncrobotic/SyncAI-Lib-HydraNet"
abstract: >-
  A multi-head perception network for fixed store CCTV, answering retail analytics and
  security questions off one camera and one forward pass. A shared RegNetX backbone and
  BiFPN neck feed independent heads — anchor-free FCOS object detection, bottom-up pose
  heatmaps decoded inside the detection boxes, and terrain segmentation — of which each
  deployment config trains the subset it needs; traversability and monocular depth heads
  remain available to configs that ask for them. Trained in PyTorch under partial
  supervision across datasets, so no single dataset has to label every task, and exported
  to ONNX for TensorRT. Anything constant on a fixed camera is measured once at
  commissioning and cached rather than learned; host-side second-stage analytics turn the
  boxes into tracks and the tracks into events on the floor in metres.
keywords:
  - computer vision
  - multi-task learning
  - object detection
  - pose estimation
  - semantic segmentation
  - cctv
  - retail analytics
  - loss prevention
  - video surveillance
license: Apache-2.0
version: 0.4.0 # x-release-please-version
